#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283596 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Element of the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3061cdb9-3f5e-578e-aa48-1b24ed90d2f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283598} {:answer/id #uuid "dd879f56-1774-57f5-bdfa-3ece34b0c42c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283599} {:answer/id #uuid "3259e6e4-8f4a-5a93-a58a-3f5ccd7b0794" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283600} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc7dec1-6220-541d-b15c-f7806182ca52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283601} {:answer/id #uuid "092a7670-38a2-597e-8b3c-c65a3e952468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd879f56-1774-57f5-bdfa-3ece34b0c42c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283599} :answer-field/id #uuid "8233a48f-b290-5757-8915-04df2ffaa58e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56f56a99-ae3f-56b5-9e3f-612f5a2d8c37" :question/math-academy-id "q-18285" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-0+(0-2) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}=\\frac{1}{-2}\\cdot (-2)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
